      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STERN EMPIRE (7) was not disgraced in some strong fields as a juvenile, and after having no favours fresh up at Ascot when racing out of her class, she was a strong finishing second at Belmont nearly 2 weeks ago. She gets a superior draw this time, and can go one better. WARDIKCAR (1) has battled on late after settling back from wide draws in his last couple of starts, and his fresh up second here is a good guide to use when considering his chances in this. Each way value from a better gate. AGENT REMINGTON (2) was unsuited by leading up last time out on this track, and it is a run best overlooked. Jason Whiting is back in the irons, and he can bounce straight back into the money here. UNIVERSAL DUKE (3) resumes from a spell and can make the most of his good draw. He has top 4 claims as well.",
